Great question! The trade-off is:

Direct embed (like Komoot): simpler code, video starts loading with the page — better for content you want visitors to see immediately
Click-to-load thumbnail: saves bandwidth on page load, but requires a click — better for performance when videos aren’t the main focus

For a blog, I’d lean toward the click-to-load approach — blog visitors tend to scan multiple posts, and lazy-loading videos keeps page loads snappy. But it’s really your call based on how you use videos in your posts.
Shall we start with the simpler approach (direct embed, matching Komoot’s pattern) and you can decide later if you want to optimize further?


