I have a bunny account. Do I need to setup a storage zone to upload file so that I can then serve them, there is the CDN but I don’t understand how to make these available, that would seem to require me to have the files on my server so that they are then loaded and made available?


🤖Reply🤖
Good question! In bunny.net, the flow is:

Storage Zone — this is where you upload your video files (like FTP). You get a storage URL and an API key/username+password.
Pull Zone — this is the CDN endpoint that serves your files to visitors. You connect it to your storage zone as the “origin”.

So the steps are:

Create a Storage Zone (e.g. my-blog-videos) — upload your .mp4 files there via FTP or their dashboard
Create a Pull Zone that pulls from that storage zone — you’ll get a CDN URL like https://my-blog-videos.b-cdn.net
Then in your blog, you can serve https://my-blog-videos.b-cdn.net/grassington.mp4

You don’t need to keep the files on your own server — bunny stores them and serves them via their CDN.
